Read object-supplied view descriptions. Render tabbed nested controls: layouts, values, text, code, editable inputs, sliders, actions, lists and tables. Invoke ordinary getters and actions, preserve typed object cells, isolate control errors, and allow editing/inspection of the backing view object.

Edit layout opens the visual designer. Update the selected tab title from the stored view definition. The recursive renderer optionally decorates each element with its node and index path so the designer shares rendering and can intercept interactions.

Read/write/invoke through live control objects; draft preview reads its chosen receiver. Poll the selected layout every second, update changed renderings and clean designers, preserve focused inputs, and stop obsolete loops.

Automatic updates preserve focused text, selection and numeric inputs while allowing updates after button clicks.


Mark the selected view tab with pressed state; display the live view title beside its inspector/layout tools. The enclosing inspector presents controls only in its Interface panel.


Place each control action result in a persistent result area across view refresh; carry its visible label to example capture.
